<title>MEXICO: Sanluis unit gets $50 mln loan.</title>
<headline>Sanluis unit gets $50 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican mining firm Sanluis Corp said on Wednesday its unit Luismin SA de CV had raised $50 million in a syndicated bank loan with a six-year maturity and a one-year grace period.</p>
<p>It said the deal was closed on Dec. 27 and Chase Manhattan Bank was lead manager. Other banks were Bank of America, Banco de Chile, Banco Inverlat, Barclays Bank and N.M. Rothschild and Sons. The interest rate was one-month LIBOR plus 225 basis points.</p>
<p>((--Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560))</p>
